<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλισθος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slipperiness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				15.14.2
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλισθον ἔχειν,</span>
			of ground, etc., to be <i>slippery,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Anach.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, Praxagorasap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλίσθημα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				150.2
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. γλώσσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.510a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Max.
			</span></i> Tyr.<i><span class="en">
				37.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>snare,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεθύουσι ὀ. οἶνος</span> Poet. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				Clem.Al.
				<u>Paed.</u>
				2.2.28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>an unknown fish with a slippery skin,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.113
			</span></i>.</div>
